      "location": "Proof 1.4",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The theorem assumes only a bounded C1 domain; the cited definition of that domain says “Connectedness is not required.” But step 1.4 infers GΩ(x,y_t)>0 from [F4], while lem-dirichlet-green-function-is-unique-and-positive requires Ω to be connected. For x and y_t in different components, the strict positivity claim need not hold (the cross-component Green function can be zero). The nonnegativity conclusion can be recovered by a componentwise argument.",
